<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="autopickup_help.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <!-- auto_pickup wildcard help (user_interface::show, ADD/EDIT rule). A passive
         backdrop stacked UNDER the string_input "Pickup Rule:" popup, replacing the
         curses help window. Static: no data model. The text is literal English with
         column alignment preserved (white-space: pre), matching the curses readout
         and the same i18n gap noted for the column heads (for the §8/F.1 sweep). -->
    <div class="panel aph-panel">
        <div class="aph-text">* is used as a Wildcard.  A few Examples:

wooden arrow    matches the itemname exactly
wooden ar*      matches items beginning with wood ar
*rrow           matches items ending with rrow
*avy fle*fi*arrow     multiple * are allowed
heAVY*woOD*arrOW      case insensitive search

Pickup using:
c:food          matches item in category food
m:kevlar        matches items made of Kevlar
M:copper        matches items made purely of copper
q:drilling      matches items with drilling qualites
k:fabrication   matches books that teach fabrication
b:c:food;*meat* matches conditions c:food and *meat*</div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
